      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Experience with 150 endovascular stents and endoprostheses including ones of vertebral and carotid arteries (first experience in Russia) is analyzed. Mini-invasive surgery is indicated for patients with isolated arterial lesions (segmental stenosis, short occlusions), changed and hard for surgery parts of vascular system (renal, visceral arteries, branches of aortic arch), restenosis after traditional surgeries and also for patients with severe concomitant diseases. Rate of complications of carotid endovascular stenting was 4,3%. The follow-up ranged from 2 months to 5,5 years. There were no restenoses in the stented zone. Complete absence of complains and regress of neurological symptoms were seen in 89% patients."},
